# Copy to .env.local if you need it. .env.local is git-ignored.
#
# You almost certainly do not. The image host is a committed constant in
# vite.config.ts, because it is a public URL that appears in every <img src>
# the site serves — not a secret, so not a variable. Dev and build both use
# it, so a fresh checkout runs and shows the real site with nothing set here.
#
# This overrides it. Two reasons to:
#
#   1. Point at somewhere else — a staging bucket, or a Pages project's own
#      .pages.dev address. Absolute URL, no trailing slash, and it must
#      include the /img suffix: the site expects everything under that
#      prefix, not the bucket root.
#
#        VITE_IMG_BASE=https://elmapt-media.pages.dev/img
#
#   2. Read the photographs off disk, for working without a network. This
#      resolves through apps/elmapt/public/res, a symlink into a local copy
#      of the media tree that is not part of a checkout — if it does not
#      resolve, the dev server says so and stops rather than starting up
#      with no photographs in it.
#
#        VITE_IMG_BASE=/res/img
#
# Do NOT set this in CI. A declared environment variable whose value turns up
# in the build output is exactly what a host's secret scanner fails on.

VITE_IMG_BASE=
